<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <Title>Stride Community Toolkit - Post Effects</Title>
        <Description>Colour transforms for Stride's post-processing chain, usable on the main camera or on a camera drawing into a texture.

What's inside:
- NightVision: luminance amplified into a green image with a soft white bloom, film grain, scanlines and a vignette
- Thermal: luminance mapped onto a false-colour ramp from cold blue through red to white-hot

Each is a ColorTransform with one small shader; add it to a PostProcessingEffects' ColorTransforms the way the engine's own Vignetting or FilmGrain are added.$(StrideVersionNote)</Description>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <Import Project="..\CommonSettings.props" />

    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- This library ships shaders. Shaders are assets compiled by the asset compiler according
             to the Graphics API target, so the package that owns the shader owns the dependency.
             Its targets also stage Effects/ into the package as stride/Assets/Effects and generate
             the matching .sdpkg manifest - do not hand-write either. -->
        <PackageReference Include="Stride.AssetCompiler" Version="$(StrideVersion)" IncludeAssets="build;buildTransitive" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Stride.CommunityToolkit\Stride.CommunityToolkit.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>